{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30223 - PROTEIN:6297",
  "verbalization": "Clavaldehyde is implicated in the inhibition of Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The evidence suggests that Clavaldehyde acts as a target of multiple compounds, all of which ultimately target Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2. Specifically, Clavaldehyde is linked to Dipeptidyl peptidase IX, which is a target of N-(3,5-dibromo-4-hydroxyphenyl)-4-hydroxy-3,5-dimethylbenzamide and Rupicolin B, both of which have been shown to inhibit Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2. Similarly, Hydroxysaikosaponin c, another compound targeting Dipeptidyl peptidase IX, also exerts a similar effect on Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2. The shared target of these compounds, Dipeptidyl peptidase IX, suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of this enzyme, which in turn affects Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Clavaldehyde and Ribosomal protein S6 kinase 2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
